# 🏡 Project Rules
- Company name must always appear as **Bliss Ventures**.
- Treat the app as a portfolio/showcase site — no backend, no APIs.
- Textual content should come from `/public/Bliss.pdf`.
- Use **online stock/placeholder images** for now (Unsplash, Pexels, etc.).
- Ensure design feels premium, modern, and professional — aligned with real estate branding.

# 🎨 Design Rules
- Primary highlight/background color: **#8b2727**
- Primary font color: **#1f2020**
- Supporting colors: light gray, white, black
- Important section titles, headers, and callouts must use **#8b2727**.
- Use Tailwind for styling — no external CSS frameworks or inline styles.
- Maintain a clean grid-based layout with plenty of whitespace.
- **Overall app width should be 90vw**, centered horizontally.
- **Each section should have a maximum height of 90vh** to maintain balance and viewport consistency.

# ⚛️ Tech Rules
- Use **Next.js with TypeScript** (`.ts`, `.tsx`).
- Use only **functional React components with hooks**.
- Static content only — no backend or database.
- Organize components into `/components` and pages into `/pages`.
- Place all static assets (PDF, images, icons) in `/public`.

# 📝 Code Style Rules
- Follow ESLint + Prettier configuration strictly.
- Use async/await where needed (though minimal for static site).
- Type all props and components with TypeScript.
- Keep components small, modular, and reusable.

# 📂 Assets & Content
- Text from `/public/Bliss.pdf` is the **source of truth**.
- Use **online placeholder real estate images** until Bliss Ventures provides official assets.
- No dummy filler text (like Lorem Ipsum).
- All content must look client-ready and consistent with branding.
